put('2-137','Sketch the corrected metallic model if the proposed drawing contains neutral atoms with electrons fixed to individual atoms. Show the particles that permit conduction.','Show a regular array of positive metal ions with delocalised electrons between them.','Positive-ion array replaces neutral-atom labels (1).|Mobile delocalised electrons replace atom-bound electrons (1).',ao=['B'])
put('5-009','Draw corrections to an electrolytic-cell sketch in which the two carbon electrodes touch, both are connected to the negative terminal, and the solution is aqueous CuSO4.','Separate the immersed electrodes and connect one to each terminal of the DC supply; label positive anode and negative cathode.','Separated immersed electrodes provide a path through electrolyte (1).|Opposite supply terminals with correct electrode labels (1).',ao=['B'])
put('6-008','Draw an energy profile from these illustrative levels: reactants 30, products 10, peak 80 kJ/mol. Label both axes, forward activation energy and ΔH.','Products lie below reactants; Ea = 50 kJ/mol upwards from reactants to peak, ΔH = −20 kJ/mol from reactants to products.','Profile matches the three levels with energy and progress axes (1).|Correct 50 kJ/mol activation and −20 kJ/mol reaction-energy arrows (1).',ao=['B'])
put('9-003','Draw particle models for two supplied solid-metal samples: P contains only copper; Q contains copper and zinc mixed within the metallic structure. Include a key.','P shows one atom type; Q shows two atom types mixed in a metallic array.','One keyed atom type for P (1).|Two keyed mixed atom types for Q (1).',ao=['B'])
put('9-005','Draw a corrected alloy model if every row is shown identical despite a key saying that one atom in four is larger. Show at least one larger atom and its local effect.','Insert larger atoms at the stated proportion in a suitable small array and distort neighbouring regular layers.','Key and larger-atom proportion represented (1).|Local layer distortion shown rather than perfectly unchanged rows (1).',ao=['B'])
put('10-055','Draw a continuing chain by joining the supplied fragments –NH–R–NH– and –C(=O)–R′–C(=O)– alternately. Mark the new linkage type.','…–NH–R–NH–C(=O)–R′–C(=O)–NH–R–NH–…; the links are amide links.','Alternating supplied fragments joined without breaking their internal structure (1).|Correct C(=O)–NH connectivity and continuation (1).',ao=['B'])
put('10-057','Draw a continuing chain by joining the supplied fragments –O–R–O– and –C(=O)–R′–C(=O)– alternately. Mark the new linkage type.','…–O–R–O–C(=O)–R′–C(=O)–O–R–O–…; the links are ester links.','Alternating supplied fragments correctly connected (1).|Correct C(=O)–O ester connectivity and continuation (1).',ao=['B'])
