put('8-038','Describe how to investigate a litmus change seen only when droplets from a warm alkaline mixture hit the paper, but not when paper is held in the gas above it.','Liquid contact can cause the change directly; repeat with damp paper in the gas while shielding it from spray.','Liquid-contact result does not establish ammonia gas (1).|Gas-only exposure with spray excluded tests the alternative (1).')
